 that implies the printed one. Lean status per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.lem-gap-mass-summability"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.lem-gap-mass-summability"],"id":"long.lem-gap-mass-summability","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Lemma 6.50 (Summability of one gap length per level)","locator":"Long record Lemma 6.50, p. 58, label lem:gap-mass-summability","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*For $n\\ge1$, put $g_n=w_n-R_n>0$. The sum of one gap length per level satisfies, for $N\\ge0$,\n$$\n\\sum_{n>N}g_n\\le\\frac29\\,4^{-N}+\\frac37\\,8^{-N}.\n$$\nThis follows by summing the per-level upper bounds geometrically. It is not the measure of the union of all gaps: level $n$ has $2^{n-1}$ translated gaps of length $g_n$. The corresponding weighted sum and its geometric interpretation are given after Theorem 6.118. Neither estimate decides membership of a specified point such as $1/2$.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.lem-gap-mass-summability","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.lem-gap-mass-summability","id":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22long.lem-gap-mass-summability%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.mersenneGap_pos%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22long.lem-gap-mass-summability%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.mersenneGap_pos%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/lean.Erdos249257.mersenneGap_pos"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.lem-gap-mass-summability","id":"sha256:f31a